.TH RFS 1 "October 2026" "rfs 3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rfs \- High-Performance Cryptographic File Splitter & Reconstructor (Post-Quantum & Plausible Deniability)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rfs
[\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILES...\fR]
.br
.B rfs split
[\fB\-n\fR \fIPARTS\fR] [\fB\-B\fR \fISIZE\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIPREFIX\fR] [\fB\-\-direct\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] \fISOURCE\fR [\fIPARTS...\fR]
.br
.B rfs restore
[\fB\-o\fR \fIDEST\fR] [\fB\-B\fR \fISIZE\fR] [\fB\-\-direct\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] \fIPART1\fR \fIPART2\fR [\fIPART3...\fR]
.br
.B rfs verify
[\fB\-B\fR \fISIZE\fR] [\fB\-\-direct\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] \fIPART1\fR \fIPART2\fR [\fIPART3...\fR]
.br
.B rfs decoy
[\fB\-c\fR \fICOUNT\fR] [\fB\-t\fR \fITEMPLATE\fR] [\fB\-s\fR \fISIZE\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIPREFIX\fR] [\fB\-B\fR \fISIZE\fR] [\fB\-\-direct\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B rfs
[\fB\-b\fR|\fB\-\-benchmark\fR]
.br
.B rfs
[\fB\-e\fR|\fB\-\-entropy\fR]
.br
.B rfs
[\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-analyze\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rfs
(Random File Splitter) is a high-performance, modular system utility designed for physical transport security,
cryptographic file splitting, and bit-accurate reconstruction.
.PP
It operates on the mathematical foundation of
.B Information-Theoretic Security via One-Time-Pad Chain (N-of-N XOR)
:
An input file or stream is split into \fIN\fR shares (\fIN\fR >= 2), where every individual share is mathematically
indistinguishable from pure white noise (Shannon entropy >= 7.9998, Chi-Square 180..330).
All \fIN\fR shares are strictly required to reconstruct the original data. If even a single share is missing,
the plaintext remains unsolvable with perfect forward secrecy.

.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B split
Splits an input file or Unix stdin stream into \fIN\fR shares.
.TP
.B restore
Reconstructs the original file or pipes it to Unix stdout from all \fIN\fR shares.
.TP
.B verify
Performs fast RAM-only integrity and BLKS-384 / SHA-256 verification without writing to disk.
.TP
.B decoy
Generates indistinguishable noise decoy files for traffic analysis resistance and multi-path obfuscation.
.TP
.B benchmark
Runs hardware throughput benchmarks measuring ChaCha20 CSPRNG streaming, AVX2/NEON SIMD-XOR, and BLKS-384 hashing.
.TP
.B entropy
Executes a two-phase hardware jitter harvest and NIST SP 800-22 diagnostic test suite.
.TP
.B analyze
Performs deep cryptographic entropy analysis and NIST SP 800-22 runs and block-frequency tests on a file.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-parts " \fINUM\fR"
Number of parts for N-way splitting (between 2 and 64; default: 2).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-decoys " \fINUM\fR"
Number of indistinguishable decoy files to generate concurrently during split.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-count " \fINUM\fR"
Number of decoy files to generate in standalone decoy subcommand (between 1 and 1000; default: 1).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-size " \fISIZE\fR"
Explicit target byte size for decoy generation (e.g., 64K, 10M, 1G).
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-template " \fIFILE\fR"
Template file for decoy generation (automatically calculates +60B stealth footer for raw files or copies 1:1 size for RFS shares).
.TP
.BR \-\-token ", " \-\-rnd
Anti-forensic random hexadecimal token mode. Generates unsequenced filename suffixes (.<rnd>.rfs) instead of numbers (.rfs1, .rfs2).
.TP
.BR \-\-pad\-to " \fISIZE\fR"
Pads all shares to an exact target byte size (e.g., 100M, 20G) using ChaCha20 random stream for size obfuscation.
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-block\-size " \fISIZE\fR"
Buffer and I/O block size (e.g., 64K, 256K, 1M, 4M, 16M; default: 4M).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIPATH\fR"
Output prefix for split shares or destination file path for restore (use '\-' for stdout).
.TP
.BR \-\-direct ", " \-\-direct\-io
Bypasses OS page cache using POSIX fadvise flags (POSIX_FADV_SEQUENTIAL and POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED) to prevent memory bloating on multi-gigabyte files.
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Emits structured machine-readable NDJSON telemetry events (\fIprogress\fR, \fIfinished\fR, \fIerror\fR) on stderr.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Overwrites existing output files without prompting.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet ", " \-\-silent
Suppresses interactive progress bars and notices; only critical errors are emitted.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Displays command-line help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Displays version information and format support.

.SH POST-QUANTUM STEALTH FOOTER (RFS3-PQ)
.B rfs
v3.0.0 embeds an in-flight 60-byte metadata footer at the tail of each share:
.IP \[bu] 2
4 Bytes: Magic identifier (\fIRFS3\fR)
.IP \[bu] 2
48 Bytes: 384-Bit Post-Quantum Merkle-Tree Hash (\fIBLKS-384\fR)
.IP \[bu] 2
8 Bytes: Little-endian original file length
.PP
The footer is cascade-XORed across all \fIN\fR shares with ChaCha20 keystream. As a result, no single share contains any magic bytes, headers, or plain text metadata.
Full backwards compatibility is maintained with historical 44-byte RFS2 SHA-256 footers.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Split a file into 3 noise shares:
.RS
.B rfs split -n 3 secret.iso
.RE
.PP
Restore the original file from 3 shares:
.RS
.B rfs restore secret.iso.rfs1 secret.iso.rfs2 secret.iso.rfs3
.RE
.PP
Stream tar archive into 4 shares over stdin:
.RS
.B tar -czf - /data | rfs split -n 4 - -o backup
.RE
.PP
Restore 4 shares directly to stdout pipe:
.RS
.B rfs restore backup.rfs* -o - | tar -xzf -
.RE
.PP
Run deep NIST SP 800-22 entropy analysis with JSON export:
.RS
.B rfs -a secret.iso.rfs1 --json
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. All shares were generated or restored with bit-accurate cryptographic integrity.
.TP
.B 1
Error occurred (integrity mismatch, missing share, invalid arguments, or I/O failure).

